                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_4">Canterbury, Kent.
                        Benedictine cathedral priory of Holy Trinity or Christ Church.
                        </orgName><p>'Iste lyber pertinet ad Bartholomeum otford monchum ecclesie
                        christi Cantuar' ordinis sancti benedicti...' and 'Thys boke pertaynythe to
                        master otford mownke of crystys churche yn canterbury anno domini mo vc xl'.
                        Otford was sub-chaplain to priory and became petty canon in 1540. See
                        Pantin, Cant. Coll. 3. 153. He was monk in 1534 (Searle, p. 156) and was
                        pensioned in 1540 (LP 15. 186).</p><p>Final leaf only.</p><p>ex Mr David
                        Pearson, Oct. 1987</p></provenance>
